    <!-- LAST, AND DELIBERATELY SO. Everything above is a dependency Core.lua asks LibStub for
         by name the moment it runs; LibDeflate is optional, and Contribute.lua already treats a
         missing one as "show the player the envelope instead of a link".

         The client stops processing the rest of an XML file when a script in it fails, so an
         optional library loaded early takes the required ones down with it -- which is exactly
         what happened: with LibDeflate second, login died on "Cannot find a library instance of
         AceTimer-3.0", an error naming a library that has nothing to do with the change.
         Ordered this way the worst case is the feature degrading, not the addon failing. -->
    <Script file="Libs\LibDeflate\LibDeflate.lua"/>
